    "exercise_name": "IFF dilemas",
    "situation_brief": "You hold a single battery defending the site, radar fixed on a 120-degree sector facing east. A mixed raid is inbound across that sector at the same time as scheduled civil traffic transits it. Magazine on the rails: 4 long-range, 5 medium-range, 4 short-range. Two rockets may be in the air at once — a third engagement cannot begin until one resolves.\n\nIdentification doctrine for tonight: IFF interrogation is available out to 200 km on any held track. A Mode 3 reply and nothing else means civil traffic — engagement prohibited, and that includes emergency codes (7500/7600/7700); an aircraft in distress is still a civil aircraft. A Mode 1 reply means a military transponder; no own-force aircraft are airborne in your sector tonight, so a Mode 1 reply is not a friendly indication. A track that answers nothing gives you no reply to read and must be judged on its flight profile. Any track still showing Unknown is a question, not a permission — refer it and expect a classification back in about fifteen seconds; fire on nothing that is not Enemy.\n\nFast closers consume the timeline. Interrogate early, classify, and take valid solutions as the system offers them.",
